## I. Context & Objective
* **Objective:** Delete src/lbfgsb_solver.{hpp,cpp}; strip all lbfgsb from c_api.cpp and r_bridge.cpp; remove lbfgs_m from structs; delete RK_ALG_LBFGSB from enum; REPLACE AUTO NOCONV/BUDGET fallback with newton_calibrate (not drop).
* **Why:** lbfgsb is strictly dominated. Replacing the AUTO fallback with newton_calibrate maintains AUTO robustness while eliminating the lbfgsb dependency.

## II. Input Specification
* **Exact changes:**

**DELETE:** src/lbfgsb_solver.hpp, src/lbfgsb_solver.cpp

**src/Makevars:3:** remove 'lbfgsb_solver.cpp'

**src/leafblower.h:**
- Line 43: delete 'RK_ALG_LBFGSB = 2,' from enum (leaves gap 0,1,3,4,... — C enums do not require contiguous values)
- Line 68: delete 'int lbfgs_m;' from rk_params_t
- Line 205: EXPECTED_RK_PARAMS_BYTES — set to 0, compile, read actual sizeof(rk_params_t), update

**src/types.hpp:119:** delete 'int lbfgs_m;' from CalibState

**src/c_api.cpp:**
- Line 4: remove '#include "lbfgsb_solver.hpp"'
- Lines 55-73: delete pack_lbfgsb_result() entirely
- Line 89: remove 'p->lbfgs_m = 10'
- Lines ~175-176: remove 'case RK_ALG_LBFGSB:' case (enum value deleted, case unreachable anyway)
- Line 244: remove 'st.lbfgs_m = p->lbfgs_m'
- Lines ~284-300: remove explicit lbfgsb dispatch block
- Lines ~284: check for 'weights_backup' — if used ONLY by the AUTO fallback, delete it too
- Lines 497-508: REPLACE (not drop) AUTO fallback:
  Old: if (status == RK_ERR_NOCONV && p->algorithm == RK_ALG_AUTO) { lbfgsb_solve... }
  New (inline the newton pack pattern, mirrors c_api.cpp existing newton block at ~line 365):
  ```cpp
  if (status == RK_ERR_NOCONV && p->algorithm == RK_ALG_AUTO) {
      if (p->verbose >= 1) st.log("auto: primary NOCONV; retrying with newton_kl");
      std::copy(weights_backup.begin(), weights_backup.end(), weights);
      auto fb = lbw::newton_calibrate(st);
      status     = fb.base.status;
      iterations = fb.base.iterations;
      max_error  = fb.base.max_error;
      used       = RK_ALG_NEWTON_KL;
      if (result) {
          result->status     = fb.base.status;
          result->iterations = fb.base.iterations;
          result->max_error  = fb.base.max_error;
          result->algorithm_used = RK_ALG_NEWTON_KL;
          // ... pack remaining fields same as explicit newton_kl block
      }
      for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) weights[i] = st.weights[i];
  }
  ```
  NOTE: weights_backup is still needed for this path (to restore weights before retry). Keep it.
- Message ternary (line ~519): remove '(used == RK_ALG_LBFGSB) ? "L-BFGS-B" :' arm

**src/r_bridge.cpp:**
- Line 20: remove '#include "lbfgsb_solver.hpp"'
- Line 43: remove '{"lbfgsb", RK_ALG_LBFGSB}' from kAlgMap
- Line 91: remove 'st.lbfgs_m = p.lbfgs_m'
- Lines ~436-441: remove explicit strcmp('lbfgsb') dispatch block
- Line 733: set kAlgNames[2] = ""  (was "L-BFGS-B"; preserve array indexing by enum value)
- Lines ~551-562: REPLACE AUTO NOCONV/BUDGET fallback:
  Old: if (res_status == RK_ERR_NOCONV || res_status == RK_ERR_BUDGET) { lbfgsb_solve... }
  New (same structure, swap solver to newton_calibrate):
  ```cpp
  if (res_status == RK_ERR_NOCONV || res_status == RK_ERR_BUDGET) {
      if (st.verbose >= 1) st.log("auto: primary NOCONV/BUDGET; retrying with newton_kl");
      std::copy(weights_backup.begin(), weights_backup.end(), weights.begin());
      auto fb = lbw::newton_calibrate(st);
      res_status     = fb.base.status;
      res_iterations = fb.base.iterations;
      res_max_error  = fb.base.max_error;
      res_alg_used   = (int)RK_ALG_NEWTON_KL;
      pack_solver_result(fb);
      if (!fb.base.best_weights.empty())
          res_best_weights = std::move(fb.base.best_weights);
      else
          res_best_weights.assign(st.n, 0.0);
  }
  ```
  NOTE: weights_backup needed here too; keep the backup copy from the AUTO block.

## III. Constraints & Guards
| Type | Guard |
| :--- | :--- |
| **weights_backup preserved** | The 'const std::vector<double> weights_backup' is needed by the newton_kl fallback. Do NOT delete it. |
| **kAlgNames[2] = ""** | Set to empty string. Preserve array structure; don't shift indices. |
| **newton_calib.hpp included** | Verify #include exists in c_api.cpp and r_bridge.cpp. |
| **Enum gap is fine** | 0,1,[2 removed],3,4,... — no code uses raw integer 2. |
| **EXPECTED_RK_PARAMS_BYTES** | Compile with 0, read error, update to actual value. |

## IV. Step-by-Step Logic
