   // 5h. Levenberg-Marquardt damped Newton: (H + μ·diag(H))·δ = G.
   //
   // Scale-invariant damping (H_aa *= (1+μ)) preserves per-coordinate scale —
   // each diag(H)_aa = p_a(1-p_a) reflects sampled cell mass for cat a, which
   // varies by orders of magnitude under severe skew. Adding μ·diag(H) (rather
   // than μ·I) interpolates Newton ↔ scaled gradient descent in each mode
   // without imposing a uniform identity floor that mismatches H's scale.
   //
